{"h":3395,"w":2400,"lines":[{"w":0.11522633870442711,"x":0.81069958772316986,"t":"Introduction","c":1,"y":0.056686046379208932,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"w":0.34773661295572916,"t":"ACADEMIC TEST FORMAT","h":0.016195524146054185,"y":0.10306242661311638,"x":0.088477372732893786,"c":1},{"x":0.088202183662383582,"t":"Listening","y":0.14000731460253768,"w":0.10764334360758462,"h":0.016750086322690039,"c":1},{"y":0.16424418589514811,"t":"This test consists of four sections, each with ten questions. The first two sections are","x":0.088477368548867993,"w":0.76337448120117191,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.18313953475078382,"h":0.01453488398216074,"w":0.81893005371093752,"x":0.088477359900207761,"t":"concerned with social needs. The first section is a conversation between two speakers and"},{"w":0.7923255411783855,"h":0.018648449186722815,"x":0.086349805399131771,"t":"the second section is a monologue. The final two sections are concerned with situations","y":0.19887464264933852,"c":1},{"t":"related to educational or training contexts. The third section is a conversation between up to","h":0.016195524146054185,"y":0.21790341564976268,"c":1,"x":0.0864197621314447,"w":0.82921808878580738},{"h":0.016026036337772664,"c":1,"y":0.23691860450344859,"w":0.4588477579752604,"t":"four people and the fourth section is a monologue.","x":0.086419742296715285},{"t":"A variety of question types is used, including: multiple choice, matching, plan\/map\/","x":0.1090535030998845,"w":0.74485595703125007,"y":0.25290697657944694,"h":0.017441860778592888,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.019338347184503668,"t":"diagram labelling, form completion, note completion, table completion, flow-chart completion,","y":0.27026027768114291,"x":0.08637700108824542,"w":0.83959284464518225},{"x":0.08634427336609643,"h":0.018822406571099459,"y":0.28849778630389167,"t":"summary completion, sentence completion and short-answer questions.","w":0.65239491780598957,"c":1},{"t":"Candidates hear the recording once only and answer the questions as they listen. Ten","h":0.018712839052449692,"w":0.77377726236979161,"c":1,"x":0.11105039780147896,"y":0.30612833641622539},{"t":"minutes are allowed at the end for candidates to transfer their answers to the answer sheet.","h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.82716049194335939,"c":1,"x":0.086419753951894718,"y":0.32412790683052961},{"w":0.093437919616699228,"t":"Reading","h":0.016882995272974544,"x":0.088182594775518625,"c":1,"y":0.35539434761987221},{"w":0.77572016398111987,"t":"This test consists of three sections with 40 questions. There are three texts, which are","y":0.37926972885474863,"h":0.017667844522968323,"x":0.086419753322378098,"c":1},{"x":0.084312931367972896,"y":0.3966267182701092,"w":0.8231514994303385,"t":"taken from journals, books, magazines and newspapers. The texts are on topics of general","c":1,"h":0.019606627339609051},{"w":0.54732508341471353,"c":1,"h":0.01598837238037687,"y":0.41569767426623849,"t":"interest. At least one text contains detailed logical argument.","x":0.086419762904380568},{"x":0.10699589602007857,"y":0.43313953472333366,"c":1,"h":0.017441860778592999,"t":"A variety of question types is used, including: multiple choice, identifying information","w":0.75925923665364592},{"w":0.8087604268391928,"h":0.018270374608124085,"c":1,"y":0.45024351500578819,"x":0.086360898864569713,"t":"(True\/False\/Not Given), identifying the writer's views\/claims (Yes\/No\/Not Given), matching"},{"w":0.81069956461588544,"t":"information, matching headings, matching features, matching sentence endings, sentence","x":0.086419764910615218,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1,"y":0.46937573598799931},{"c":1,"t":"completion, summary completion, note completion, table completion, flow-chart completion,","x":0.086419745808517329,"w":0.8251028951009115,"h":0.017498356714686691,"y":0.48691860449101787},{"h":0.017738919656886121,"c":1,"t":"diagram label completion and short-answer questions.","y":0.50418884234480665,"w":0.49395833333333328,"x":0.086344672868533506},{"x":0.084798383638970548,"t":"Writing","h":0.022690884216092888,"w":0.083807563781738287,"c":1,"y":0.53171337084091064},{"y":0.55948174313224519,"t":"This test consists of two tasks. It is suggested that candidates spend about 20 minutes on","x":0.086419756784025595,"w":0.80864196777343755,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1},{"y":0.57617166244513274,"t":"Task 1, which requires them to write at least 150 words, and 40 minutes on Task 2, which","x":0.086367363856257956,"h":0.01990386369792807,"c":1,"w":0.8046284993489583},{"c":1,"x":0.084273626240636765,"w":0.82937052408854173,"t":"requires them to write at least 250 words. Task 2 contributes twice as much as Task 1 to the","h":0.018134461976894944,"y":0.59390455811282683},{"t":"Writing score.","w":0.13058333079020182,"x":0.085958673098685906,"y":0.61400228183036454,"h":0.016810619367727542,"c":1},{"h":0.017513764901492479,"c":1,"x":0.10699589032218522,"y":0.63074204920569543,"t":"Task 1 requires candidates to look at a diagram or some data (in a graph, table or chart)","w":0.79629628499348959},{"c":1,"t":"and to present the information in their own words. They are assessed on their ability to","x":0.086419744351222696,"w":0.77983540852864597,"y":0.64811542991065874,"h":0.016195524146054074},{"c":1,"y":0.66715116263155694,"h":0.017477812840042684,"t":"organise, present and possibly compare data, and are required to describe the stages of a","x":0.086419747651204096,"w":0.81275721232096365},{"w":0.64003367106119791,"c":1,"y":0.68399240510685633,"h":0.018256953523633657,"t":"process, describe an object or event, or explain how something works.","x":0.084299324308499832},{"t":"In Task 2, candidates are presented with a point of view, argument or problem. They are","c":1,"x":0.10493827726508309,"y":0.70200235585057991,"h":0.017474388486504955,"w":0.7962962849934897},{"w":0.82921808878580727,"y":0.72084805635171123,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"x":0.084362148938411111,"t":"assessed on their ability to present a solution to the problem, present and justify an opinion,"},{"t":"compare and contrast evidence and opinions, and to evaluate and challenge ideas, evidence","y":0.73837209286332306,"h":0.0175171886933847,"x":0.084362138907207798,"w":0.83950617472330735,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"or arguments.","y":0.75872093007034525,"w":0.13168724060058595,"h":0.01454173212759069,"x":0.084362141061310181},{"w":0.74297134399414066,"c":1,"t":"Candidates are also assessed on their ability to write in an appropriate style. More","x":0.10690933595704223,"y":0.77197838798708096,"h":0.018558521854863397},{"h":0.016031172025610885,"c":1,"x":0.082304517856146051,"y":0.79210836299959653,"t":"information on assessing the Writing test, including Writing assessment criteria (public","w":0.77983540852864586},{"y":0.80897738386906715,"c":1,"t":"version), is available on the IELTS website.","x":0.084251044588491239,"h":0.018442322424359614,"w":0.39524085998535158},{"x":0.9074074074418873,"w":0.016460905075073251,"c":1,"h":0.014534883982160851,"t":"5","y":0.92877906951570255},{"w":0.20824633280436194,"y":0.96768258536995222,"x":0.39483721299237268,"h":0.016454192297478354,"c":1,"t":"leltsresources.org"}]}